    relatedProgramIds: ["feeling-and-relating"],
    signoffRowIds: ["CV10_A11"],
    body: "## The idea\nHard experiences, especially ones involving other people, can change how safe closeness feels. You might want connection and also feel wary of it. You might expect to be let down, find it hard to ask for things, or keep people at a distance.\n\n## Why it makes sense\nThese patterns are usually lessons your mind learned to protect you. They made sense then. The question now is whether they still fit the people in your life today.\n\n## What helps\nSmall, low-stakes moments of connection, with people who have shown they're reasonably safe, help build trust gradually. So does practicing saying what you need in small ways. There's no need to go faster than feels okay.\n\n## A small practice\nTry \"Who's actually there\" to notice the support around you, even if it's small.",
