    relatedModuleIds: [],
    signoffRowIds: ["CV10_A12"],
    body: "## The idea\nEveryone reaches for ways to feel better fast. Some of those ways, like drinking, scrolling for hours, overworking, avoiding people, or using substances, bring quick relief but make things harder over time.\n\n## Why it happens\nThese habits work, briefly. That's why they stick. Needing relief isn't a flaw. It's a sign that something hurts.\n\n## What helps\nRather than trying to stop everything at once, it helps to add options. Having a few quick, healthier ways to ease strong feelings makes it easier to choose them sometimes. Noticing the urge and riding it out, even once, builds that skill.\n\n## A small practice\nTry \"Ride the urge\" the next time you feel a pull toward a habit that costs you. If you're worried about your use of alcohol or drugs, a doctor or counselor can help, and it's okay to ask.",
