    relatedProgramIds: ["moving-toward"],
    signoffRowIds: ["CV10_A13"],
    body: "## The idea\nWhen mood is low, it's natural to wait until you feel like doing things. But low mood tends to shrink what we do, and doing less tends to lower mood further. It becomes a loop.\n\n## Flipping the order\nOne of the most practical ways out of that loop is to act first, in small ways, and let the feeling follow. Not big changes. Small, doable steps connected to things you care about.\n\n## What counts\nAnything that gives a small sense of getting something done, of enjoyment, or of connection. Opening a window counts. Replying to one message counts. So does ten minutes on something you used to enjoy.\n\n## What to expect\nAt first, activities may not feel as good as they used to. That's normal. The good feelings often come back gradually as you keep going.\n\n## A small practice\nThink of one thing you could do in the next day that would take less than ten minutes.",
